{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Because your Elohim.</b> The lamed with בין, and the bet alone [ב] would suffice, or the word בין:" "<b>He hid His face from you.</b> Like the language of a human being who hides his face and his ears so that he neither sees nor hears:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 59, :notes {0 "The comment addresses the prefixed lamed on לבין in Isaiah 59:2; Ibn Ezra notes it may be redundant alongside בין."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:12.901729472Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}